A||N||11||Manta||Please Help...No Speedometer||||5||
Z||000000||Manta||05-16-2000||10:40 PM||||Last weekend I bought a 1986 1/2 Fiero GT. 2.8 liter V6. 80,000 miles. Not much wrong except the Servce Engine Soon light would come on, the the air doesn't blow cold, and the Speedometer & Odometer both do not work. I checked the Vehicle Speed Sensor and it puts out A.C. Volts and max. out at 4.95 Vac at high R.P.M s. (That's Normal, Right?)<BR>I then swaped out the gauge cluster and still nothing. Today I put in a new ECM and my Service Engine light is now working normal but still no Speed or Odometer. Some people have told me that the E-Prom is bad and then others have said if it was I would have more problems then this. My manual say's the E-Prom does control the air and speedometer but I don't want to buy one if that's not it. Any ideas what to check next?||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||05-16-2000||10:53 PM||||Check the "radio" fuse on the fuse block under the dash. I'm serious.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Manta||05-16-2000||11:32 PM||||Thanks but I checked every fuse. All were good.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||05-17-2000||06:49 AM||||I'm quite sure that the computer does not control the speedo. the signal comes from the vss to the speedo then to the computer. 4000 pulses/mile to the speedo then 2000 pulses/mile to the computer. Does the ECM give a vss input error code?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Manta||05-17-2000||10:01 AM||||I do not own a scanner to check the codes on the ECM. The only mechanic in town that has one is charging $75.00 just to plug in and read me the code. So I guess I am stuck shot gunning it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Linx||05-17-2000||10:23 AM||||No dude- you can <I>check your own codes!</I>  If you short two pins on the diagnostics connector, the 'check engine' light will flash the code sequence!<P>The codes are in the Haynes Manual.  And this link, too...<P> <A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/fiero.htm</A> <P>The connector is behind the cigarette lighter panel.  With engine off and key on, get a wire jumper and connect the two bottom left hand pins together.  The ecm will start flashing codes..count em.  flash &gt;pause&lt; flash-flash &gt;pause&lt; is a code 12.  Get it?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Manta||05-17-2000||12:53 PM||||Ok I jumpered he wire and the only code was 12. With this result can I assume that it is not the E-Prom?||||reg||1
Z||000007||mwbackus||05-17-2000||01:40 PM||||I have seen this before on a car that the previous owner did a "cut" wire trick.  He did this to disable the odometer so he could drive around with "undocumented" miles before he sold the car.  The guy that bought this particular car had to sue to get his money back from the jerk.  <BR>I would do a little wire tracing with a digital OHM meter to determine if this is the case.<P>Mike B.||||reg||9
Z||000008||Manta||05-17-2000||01:58 PM||||Thanks, That was going to be my next move.<BR>NEW QUESTION: Something I didn't mention before, The Cruse Control also doesn't work. Does anyone know if in someway this could interupt the signal to the dash?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Phil||05-17-2000||04:32 PM||||Cruise signal comes from the dash||||reg||1
Z||000010||DRH||05-17-2000||04:40 PM||||The "flow" is from the VSS to the speedometer board. The speedometer board drives the spedometer and odometer directly. It also sends an output to the ECM and the CC module. <P>Whatever is causing the speedo problem is probably also keeping the cruise from working.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Manta||05-19-2000||09:48 PM||||NEW UPDATE: This is getting strange.I just got back from a 500 mile 2 day drive. at about 250 miles everything started working. I didn't hit any rough roads or bumps. Then of all things 34 miles later I got a hole on a radiator hose and the engine got realy hot.While I was coasting a half mile to a rest area the speedo stopped reading then started then stopped about 5 times then dead again.I taped up the hose and drove it the other 250 miles but it never came on again.<BR>Could the heat of the engine knock out anything that controls the speedo or would it have gone out at that point anyway?||||reg||1
